    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280007": {
      "title": "Coadjutant Non-Teaching",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Coadjutant Non-Teaching Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Coadjutant Non-Teaching Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Coadjutant Non-Teaching Department Mechanical & Aerospace Eng Salary Details $6000 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, based on position, which includes: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits Life insurance coverage Employee discounts programs For detailed information on benefits and eligibility, please visit: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/benefits/benefits-overview . Posting Summary Looking for a candidate that can Oversee the operation and coordination of the Packaging Engineering laboratories, including laboratory facilities, equipment, and laboratory instructional activities. Responsibilities include ensuring that laboratories are properly maintained, equipment is operational and available for teaching safety procedures are followed, and laboratory resources effectively support the Packaging Engineering curriculum. Coordinate with faculty, staff, and students regarding laboratory needs, equipment use, maintenance, and improvements. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 26FA0711 Posting Open Date 08/17/2026 Posting Close Date 01/31/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience An MS or PhD in Packaging Engineering, Materials, Industrial or Mechanical Engineering. Experience in the Packaging Engineering field with an understanding of the future AI and Automation benefits, impacts, and challenges in the Circular Economy encompassing sustainability, economics, technology, legislation and infrastructure. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Undergraduate education and experience in areas related to the described position description Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279518 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Busch (RU-New Brunswick) City Piscatawy State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunizati