s options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary Freeman Lab is seeking for a summer assistant to aid with laboratory-based engineering and biomedical engineering research activities related to virtual laboratory development, AI-supported engineering learning environments, multimodal analysis activities, and community engagement initiatives. Responsibilities include assisting with experimental setup, operation of laboratory equipment, software utilization and data analysis, support of multimodal physiological response analysis activities, technical documentation, review and piloting of curricular materials, and support of outreach and educational activities designed to expand student engagement in engineering and STEM learning experiences. Position Status Part Time Posting Number 26FA0538 Posting Open Date Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Some high school experience necessary. Must have experience with Microsoft Excel and several data analysis software packages. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities High school senior-level writing, expertise in data analysis software Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Sitting at a desk, moving around a lab to engage experiment participants. Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276165 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Busch (RU-New Brunswick) City Piscataway State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, 