d contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking non-credit part time instructors for the Center for Mathematics, Science, and Computer Education. We seek qualified instructors who can contribute to the University’s educational mission and bridge the gap between the classroom and the industry. Successful candidates will instruct/co-instruct on a wide variety of topics in K-12 STEM education. Candidates will be responsible for the following: • Instructing/co-instructing mathematics, STEM , STEAM , maker education, or coding workshops for teachers and/or students at the K-12 level • Prepare course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.) • Provide constructive feedback to participants. • Practice innovative educational methodology Position Status Part Time Posting Number 26FA0063 Posting Open Date 01/23/2026 Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Requires a Masters/PhD. degree in K-12 Mathematics or STEM field and at least two years of K-12 instructional experience. Also requires excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Individual will have knowledge of classroom management, adult learning, and effective communication/facilitation techniques. We are an inclusive learning community, and classroom spaces should reflect that, regardless of subject matter. Success in this position will be measured through workshop enrollment attendance, evaluations, and participant engagement. Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Must be willing to travel since workshops are offered throughout New Jersey. Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https: