ution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Rutgers Business School invites applications for Course Assistants for the calendar year 2026 semester (Spring, Summer, and Fall 2026). Successful candidates will be responsible for, but not limited to, the following: Assisting faculty with their course(s) (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online courses); may be required to provide LMS software assistance Attending all assigned course meetings (at the discretion of the faculty member teaching the course) Preparing course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.) as directed by the faculty member Providing constructive feedback to students as well as critical instruction regarding student work and academic standards Responding to student emails and inquiries and addressing student concerns Practicing innovative educational methodology Assisting with research assignments Proctoring course exams, if applicable and approved by the faculty member Position Status Part Time Posting Number 25FA1260 Posting Open Date 12/01/2025 Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience as a teaching/course assistant. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview The Rutgers Business School ( RBS ) is a key leader in business education, offering undergraduate and graduate programs that not only teach our students to excel in their field of study but also inspire them to create a positive social impact. We offer degree programs in the fields of Accounting, Business Analytics and Information Technology, Finance, Management, Management Science and Information Systems, 