retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Department seeks applications for two one-year, possibly-renewable teaching positions at the rank of NTT Lecturer at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor available beginning January 1, 2026, subject to the availability of funding, with the possibility of appointment at a higher level for well-qualified candidates. This position has a teaching load of 4-4 (four undergraduate mathematics courses in each of the fall and spring semesters), with possible teaching reductions for administrative, advising or other departmental duties. Applicants should have received a Ph.D. and show outstanding evidence of teaching at the undergraduate level. Ideally, candidates will have had at least three years teaching experience by the time the position starts. The academic year salary for an assistant resp. associate resp. full teaching professor will not be less than $82,110 based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union ( AAUP - AFT ) and Rutgers University. Applicants should complete the online form associated with this listing and submit a curriculum vitae. In addition, you should register as a job applicant at mathjobs.org https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/27867 and complete the application, with the requested supporting documents, for position TF26B under the Rutgers University-New Brunswick listing. Review of applications begins on December 22, 2025. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 25FA1243 Posting Open Date Posting Close Date Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience A PhD in Mathematics, or equivalent, is preferred; a BA in Mathematics or related field is required. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265231 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Busch (RU-New Brunswick) City Piscataway State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following 