    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/283172": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Associate",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Post Doctoral Associate Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Post Doctoral Associate Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Post Doctoral Associate Department Materials Science & Engineerg Salary Details $63,968 Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary Responsible for conducting research on materials for extreme conditions, especially boride- and carbide-based ceramics. It is expected that the person will be familiar with methods used in the synthesis, processing and characterization of materials, and be able to use computational software for materials simulation. Knowledge of high temperature furnaces, hot presses, powder processing, and additive manufacturing will be of particular value. The person will assist graduate students in the program with the synthesis, processing, characterization and computational simulation of the ceramic materials. They will be expected to present and write research papers on the conducted research, collaborate with industrial partners and the Army research laboratory, and oversee process and characterization laboratories. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0955 Posting Open Date 11/02/2026 Posting Close Date 11/09/2026 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience PhD in Materials Science and Engineering, Ceramics Engineering or closely related discipline is a prerequisite. Must have demonstrated record of using Material Characterization and Processing. Must have experience in Stereolithography Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/283165 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Busch (RU-New Brunswick) City Piscataway State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employmen