    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/283156": {
      "title": "Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty position",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty position Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty position Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty position Department Computer Science Salary Details The academic year salary will not be less than $82,110, based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union (AAUP-AFT) and Rutgers University Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, based on position, which includes: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits Life insurance coverage Employee discounts programs For detailed information on benefits and eligibility, please visit: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/benefits/benefits-overview . Posting Summary The Computer Science Department at Rutgers University, New Brunswick NJ, invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track teaching faculty position. We are searching for an Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor, but will consider excellent applicants at all ranks. We seek dedicated educators able to teach a broad range of courses, including introductory programming, data structures, discrete structures, computer architecture and systems, algorithms, artificial intelligence, and cybersecurity. Computer Science is a large undergraduate major in the School of Arts and Sciences, and we are especially interested in innovative approaches to teaching, including active learning, thoughtful integration of AI tools in education, and courses that scale to large student populations. Located in New Jersey, Rutgers University is a premier, Research 1, public land grant institution that reflects the broad spectrum of backgrounds in the state. The School of Arts and Sciences, the largest and most comprehensive school at Rutgers University, is especially interested in candidates who can advance the goals and values expressed in the SAS Strategic Plan . Applicants are encouraged to include in their cover letter information about how they will further our mission of excellence. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, including those with non-traditional career paths or who have achieved excellence in careers outside academia. Teaching faculty have a promotion ladder through Distinguished Teaching Professor and presumptively renewable appointments governed by the collective bargaining agreement, and are voting members of the department and the school. The academic year salary will not be less than $82,110, based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union ( AAUP - AFT ) and Rutgers University, and will be commensurate with rank and experience. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate Computer Science courses, developing course materials and assessments, supervising recitation instructors and graders, curriculum development, and student advising. Opportunities to teach in the Master’s program may be available depending on experience and are subject to negotiation. The standard teaching load is five courses per year, which can be reduced for negotiated research or service duties. Requirements: A Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field is required by the start date. Candidates for senior ranks should have a record of teaching excellence and educational leadership commensurate with rank. Timeline: The appointment will start September 1, 2027. Applications received by December 15, 2026, will be given priority. How to Apply: Applicants should submit their cover letter, CV, a teaching statement including evidence of teaching effectiveness, and contact information for at least three references, at least one of whom can speak to the candidate’s teaching. For details, including application procedure, please see: https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/282392 Contact Info: ntt-hiring@cs.rutgers.edu Rutgers Policies: Offer is contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Rutgers is an equal opportunity employer: see http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0932 Posting Open Date 10/19/2026 Posting Close Date 03/31/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience A Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field is required by the start date. Candidates for senior ranks should have a record of teaching excellence and educational leadership commensurate with rank Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement The appointment will start September 1, 2027. Applications received by December 15, 2026, will be given priority. Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/282392 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Busch (RU-New Brunswick) City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the institution and year of graduation for the PhD degree of the candidate? (Open Ended Question) If the candidate has teaching experience, how many years and where? (Open Ended Question) If the candidate has industry experience, how many years and where? (Open Ended Question) If available, provide any webpage link that highlights a teaching portfolio: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of Professional References (contact Info) Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Teaching Interests Personal Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: Non-Discrimination-Statement . In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination (NJLAD), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation with regard to your access to and/or your participation in the application and selection processes (for example, the online application process or interviews), please call 848-932-3973 or e-mail us . Rutgers University is an equal access/equal opportunity institution. If you have trouble accessing this page because of a disability, please contact us at 732.745.7378 or via email at OneSource@Rutgers.edu . Rutgers University participates in the E-Verify program as required by law. Learn more about the E-Verify program . For technical assistance with the applicant tracking system (login, filling out your application, resetting your password, etc.) please contact the ROCS Help Desk at 848-932-4444 or ROCS@hr.rutgers.edu . To learn more about Rutgers University’s commitment to diversity and inclusion on its campuses, click here . Copyright © 2014 , Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution. Contact RU-info at 732-445-info (4639) | Questions? Ask Colonel Henry or text us at 732-662-2664. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/283155": {
      "title": "Professor of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies",
      "description": "Rutgers University Employment Opportunities | Professor of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Skip to Main Content Universitywide | New Brunswick | Newark | Camden | RBHS University Search University Human Resources Home Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Why Work at Rutgers? Rutgers Edge The RU Commitment Benefits Information Information for New Employees URA-AFT Job Postings Rutgers University Foundation Job Postings Professor of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Recruitment/Posting Title Professor of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Department Women's Gender & Sexuality Salary Details The academic year salary will not be less than $82,110 for an Assistant Professor; Associate Professor no less than $84,950; or Full Professor no less than $95,764, based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union (AAUP-A Offer Information The final salary offer may be determined by several factors, including, but not limited to, the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and expertise, and availability of department or grant funds to support the position. We also take into consideration market benchmarks, if and when appropriate, and internal equity to ensure fair compensation relative to the university’s broader compensation structure. We are committed to offering competitive and flexible compensation packages to attract and retain top talent. Benefits Rutgers provides a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. The specific benefits vary based on the position and may include: Medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits (when applicable) Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Posting Summary The Department of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies ( WGSS ) at Rutgers University-New Brunswick invites applications for an open-rank, tenured or tenure-track professor of women’s, gender, and sexuality studies, to begin September 1, 2027. We seek a candidate with a strong background in women’s, gender and sexuality studies, with field specialization in Global Black Feminisms. We welcome interdisciplinary candidates from a range of humanistic and humanist social science backgrounds whose interests include but are not limited to Global South and transnational feminist diasporas, transnational feminist visual and sonic cultures and cultural production, feminist digital cultures and technologies, social movements and activism, critical sexualities, gender-based violence, disability studies, ecofeminism, and feminisms and religion. We are interested in scholars who can teach courses such as Black Feminist Theory, Comparative Feminism, Gender and Popular Culture, Gender, Race, and Visual Media, and our range of graduate proseminars. Located in New Jersey, Rutgers University is a premiere, Research 1, public land grant institution that reflects the broad spectrum of backgrounds in the state. The School of Arts and Sciences, the largest and most comprehensive school at Rutgers University, is especially interested in candidates who can advance the goals and values expressed in the SAS Strategic Plan . Applicants are encouraged to include in their cover letter information about how they will further our mission of excellence. Qualified candidates must hold a Ph.D. in a relevant field, along with a developed research agenda and record of publications commensurate with the rank of the position being applied for. The full-time position comes with a 2-2 teaching load, and duties include teaching, advising, and service contributions within the Department of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies. For full consideration all materials must be received by December 1, 2026. Please submit a cover letter that includes research and teaching experience, curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for three references who may be asked to submit letters of recommendation. Documents can be uploaded through the UHR system. Candidates may be asked to provide a writing sample at a future stage of the search committee’s evaluation of files. Position Status Full Time Posting Number 26FA0949 Posting Open Date 10/26/2026 Posting Close Date 01/15/2027 Qualifications Minimum Education and Experience Qualified candidates must hold a Ph.D. in a relevant field, along with a developed research agenda and record of publications commensurate with the rank of the position being applied for. Certifications/Licenses Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Preferred Qualifications Equipment Utilized Physical Demands and Work Environment Overview Statement Posting Details Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/282724 Campus Rutgers University-New Brunswick Home Location Campus Rutgers University - New Brunswick City New Brunswick State NJ Location Details Douglass Campus Pre-employment Screenings All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of all pre-employment screenings. Immunization Requirements Under Policy 100.3.1 Immunization Policy for Covered Individuals , if employment will commence during Flu Season, Rutgers University may require certain prospective employees to provide proof that they are vaccinated against Seasonal Influenza for the current Flu Season, unless the University has granted the individual a medical or religious exemption. Additional infection control and safety policies may apply. Prospective employees should speak with their hiring manager to determine which policies apply to the role or position for which they are applying. Failure to provide proof of vaccination for any required vaccines or obtain a medical or religious exemption from the University will result in rescission of a candidate’s offer of employment or disciplinary action up to and including termination. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of Professional References (contact Info) Optional Documents It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: Non-Discrimination-Statement . In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination (NJLAD), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation with regard to your access to and/or your participation in the application and selection processes (for example, the online application process or interviews), please call 848-932-3973 or e-mail us . Rutgers University is an equal access/equal opportunity institution. If you have trouble accessing this page because of a disability, please contact us at 732.745.7378 or via email at OneSource@Rutgers.edu . Rutgers University participates in the E-Verify program as required by law. Learn more about the E-Verify program . For technical assistance with the applicant tracking system (login, filling out your application, resetting your password, etc.) please contact the ROCS Help Desk at 848-932-4444 or ROCS@hr.rutgers.edu . To learn more about Rutgers University’s commitment to diversity and inclusion on its campuses, click here . Copyright © 2014 , Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution. Contact RU-info at 732-445-info (4639) | Questions? Ask Colonel Henry or text us at 732-662-2664. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
